CORE
main.c
module.c --validate-goto-model --validate-ssa-equation
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
^.*unexpected difference between type symbols.*$
^Invariant check failed$
--
`struct ring` contains an anonymous union whose synthetic tag identifier
encodes whether `struct inner` was complete, so main.c and module.c give the
same C type two different anonymous-union tags.  The linker accepts the two
`struct ring` definitions as structurally equivalent and keeps main.c's.  It
must then also map module.c's anonymous-union tag to main.c's one; otherwise
the struct value built in module.c has a component whose type disagrees with
the kept `struct ring`, which tripped type invariants during symex
(simplify_member: "member expression type must match component type").
